{"kind":"assert","text":"ARC-1 measurement boundary, answer to 7bd09354. Measure the widest change/propose-manifest shape that actually seals. The 99-fact static bound is not the boundary if Native refuses it before sealing, so take the widest local-hold shape, with your matched control, archive it under the unchanged budget, and record the charge on each limit axis.\n\nOne question needs a separate answer, because it may be a defect rather than a bound: can any J4 foreign-hold propose-manifest seal, at any width? Run the narrowest legitimate foreign-hold case. If it also refuses required-unset, file that as its own finding against J4 with the native log, and do not fold it into ARC-1. If narrow cases seal and only wide ones refuse, give the width where refusal starts. That width then bounds what the archive must handle.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}